    "definition": "Fixedn=m4,d3 complex Hermitian PSD matrices, minimize mean of256 Frobenius product norms divided by mean of24 distinct-index product norms; positive denominator. Norm is inside each summation. Rational Hermitian matrices with positive-definite perturbations preserve infimum.",
    "primary_source": "AlphaEvolve2511.02864v1 section6.47 explicitly states m>=4 open and lists(4,4,3) and Schatten2 tests. Duchi2012 inside-sum variant and Israel/Krahmer/Ward2016 proof for3 distinguished from RechtRe outside-sum counterexamples and2026 outside-sum claims.",
    "human_and_reference": "Four identity matrices give exact1 by the traditional equality case explicitly stated in primary source. This is a feasible upper bound on the infimum, not a proved minimum. Failed AI searches in source are not optimality evidence.",
    "independent_method": "Root Symbolic SymPy matrices independently verify all principal minors, every ordered product, and trace(M.H*M). Finer rational root enclosures certify every interval. Additional unequal diagonal and noncommuting complex fixtures give ratios about1.19204425349 and1.25270204220; both checked independently, recorded under runs/sol_additional_noncommuting_20261106.json.",
    "admission": "All five entries attain1, identity ratios cancel exactly. Root reruns all required strict controls, invalid negative minor, full-return claim invariance, saved replay, cold export, and program-error/nonfinite/timeout. Checker has no arbitrary coefficient-precision cap."
  }
